messages.content:
Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: apps/ocsp.c
Line: 476
Function: ocsp_main
Bug type: double-free
CWE: CWE-415
Explanation: In the -issuer option handling, the loaded certificate 'issuer' is pushed onto the 'issuers' stack (sk_X509_push(issuers, issuer)) but 'issuer' is not set to NULL afterwards. If later cleanup frees both the individual 'issuer' pointer and also frees the elements of 'issuers' (common in OpenSSL apps via sk_X509_pop_free), the same X509 object will be freed twice, causing a double free.

